title: UAC Bypass via COM Elevation Moniker
id: 24da16a4-cc09-48bd-b1ed-c4ee4538b119
status: experimental
description: Detects UAC bypass through auto-elevated COM objects (ICMLuaUtil, CMSTPLUA), indicated by dllhost.exe with a suspicious /Processid CLSID spawning an elevated child, used to run commands without a UAC prompt.
author: Alaris Global
references:
  - https://attack.mitre.org/techniques/T1548/002/
logsource:
  product: windows
  category: process_creation
detection:
  selection:
    ParentImage|endswith: '\\dllhost.exe'
    Image|endswith:
      - '\\cmd.exe'
      - '\\powershell.exe'
    IntegrityLevel:
      - 'High'
      - 'System'
  condition: selection
fields:
  - CommandLine
  - Image
  - ParentImage
falsepositives:
  - Rare legitimate elevated COM usage
level: high
tags:
  - attack.privilege_escalation
  - attack.t1548.002
